event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"id":"mcp_08f104d4ec2b32e4006abb8d3aac2c87d2801c2f8bd76d7010","type":"mcp_call","status":"completed","approval_request_id":"mcpr_08f104d4ec2b32e4006abb8d3a067887d289073a0b6410cea5","arguments":"{\"repoName\":\"cequence-io/openai-scala-client\",\"question\":\"Which ws-client version does this project depend on?\"}","error":null,"name":"ask_wiki_question","output":"The project `cequence-io/openai-scala-client` depends on `ws-client` version `1.0.0` . This version is defined in the `Dependencies.scala` file  and used across various modules like `openai-core` , `openai-client` , and `anthropic-client` .\n\n## `ws-client` Version Definition\n\nThe `ws-client` version is centrally defined in `project/Dependencies.scala`  within the `Versions` object  as `val wsClient = \"1.0.0\"` .\n\n## Usage Across Modules\n\nThis `wsClient` version is then imported and used in the `build.sbt` files of different modules:\n*   **`openai-core`**: It depends on `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-core-akka\" % wsClient`  and `\"io.cequence\" %% \"json-repair\" % wsClient` .\n*   **`openai-client`**: It uses `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-core\" % wsClient`  and `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka\" % wsClient` .\n*   **`anthropic-client`**: This module depends on `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-core\" % wsClient` , `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka\" % wsClient` , and `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka-stream\" % wsClient` .\n*   **`google-vertexai-client`**: It includes `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-core\" % wsClient`  and `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka\" % wsClient` .\n*   **`openai-client-stream`**: This module also uses `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-core\" % wsClient` , `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka\" % wsClient` , and `\"io.cequence\" %% \"ws-client-play-akka-stream\" % wsClient` .\n\n## Notes\nThe `CHANGELOG.md` file also mentions the migration to `io.cequence:ws-client-*:1.0.0` , indicating that this version is a significant update with changes to how engines are handled and shared across services . The `.scala-steward.conf` file explicitly ignores updates for `groupId = \"io.cequence\"` , suggesting that `ws-client` is a sibling library managed manually via coordinated releases .\n\nWiki pages you might want to explore:\n- [Module Architecture (cequence-io/openai-scala-client)](/wiki/cequence-io/openai-scala-client#1.2)\n- [Service Factories and Configuration (cequence-io/openai-scala-client)](/wiki/cequence-io/openai-scala-client#4)\n\nView this search on DeepWiki: https://deepwiki.com/search/which-wsclient-version-does-th_28a624d4-780d-476f-a849-59694c9ba371\n","server_label":"deepwiki"},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":7}

